<https://hexplain.io/ns/video> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Semantic vocabulary for video stream and container properties."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for video containers, streams, tracks and timing metadata. Nominal rate must not be used as an exact variable-rate timeline."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Interlaced> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Scanning convention in which successive fields carry different line subsets of an image frame."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Interlaced> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for video containers, streams, tracks and timing metadata. Nominal rate must not be used as an exact variable-rate timeline. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Interlaced> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/video> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#PositiveAspectRatioShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Positive Aspect Ratio. Both aspect-ratio components must be positive."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#PositiveAspectRatioShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using vdv:aspectRatio Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#PositiveAspectRatioShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Positive Aspect Ratio Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#PositiveAspectRatioShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/video> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Progressive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Scanning convention in which a frame represents a full image rather than alternating interlaced fields."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Progressive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use for video containers, streams, tracks and timing metadata. Nominal rate must not be used as an exact variable-rate timeline. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#Progressive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/video> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#RateShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for vdv:frameRateDenominator, vdv:frameRateNumerator. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/video#RateShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using vdv:frameRateDenominator, vdv:frameRateNumerator Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
